Package: lexsync
Type: Package
Title: Multidimensional Lexical Optimisation and Hardware-Timed Experiment Generation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Pablo", "Bernabeu", email = "pcbernabeu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A cross-platform toolkit that unifies many-language lexical-corpus
    access, parallel multidimensional stimulus matching, counterbalancing and the
    automated generation of hardware-timed 'PsychoPy' and 'OpenSesame' experiment
    scripts for electroencephalography and event-related potential research. It is
    the R member of a dual-language pair; a structurally identical 'Python' package
    is also provided. Stimuli are matched across several lexical dimensions (length,
    frequency, orthographic neighbourhood density and OLD20) by a deterministic
    tolerance-and-nearest-neighbour procedure, and onset triggers are bound to the
    stimulus flip in the generated 'PsychoPy' scripts.
